&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">1
&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>ssh -T git@github.com
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>&lt;/tr>&lt;/table>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;p>still times out or fails.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="root-cause--ssh-does-not-use-the-http-proxy--key-point">&lt;strong>Root cause — SSH does NOT use the HTTP proxy&lt;/strong> (key point)&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Terminal HTTP/SOCKS environment variables affect HTTP/HTTPS-aware programs (curl, wget, &lt;code>git clone https://…&lt;/code>, etc.), but &lt;strong>OpenSSH does not honor those variables&lt;/strong>. SSH opens a raw TCP connection and must be explicitly told to use a proxy — otherwise it tries a direct connection and gets blocked by the network/firewall.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Root配置全体用户均可用的代理</title><link>https://jzjizhe.github.io/tool/root%E9%85%8D%E7%BD%AE%E5%85%A8%E4%BD%93%E7%94%A8%E6%88%B7%E5%9D%87%E5%8F%AF%E7%94%A8%E7%9A%84%E4%BB%A3%E7%90%86/</link><pubDate>Wed, 22 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://jzjizhe.github.io/tool/root%E9%85%8D%E7%BD%AE%E5%85%A8%E4%BD%93%E7%94%A8%E6%88%B7%E5%9D%87%E5%8F%AF%E7%94%A8%E7%9A%84%E4%BB%A3%E7%90%86/</guid><description>&lt;p>&lt;strong>The note is generated by chatGPT.&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
